-- title:
--   Non-unipotent inertia and Steinberg Frobenius for newform representations
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $M$, a weight-two cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform (a normalised eigenform in the sense that $a_1(g)=1$ with the multiplicative and prime-power recursions for the $q$-coefficients, and whose eigensystem on primes away from $M$ is not matched by a normalised eigenform of any proper divisor level), a prime $\lambda$ with $\lambda \neq 2$, a finite set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, and a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring $O'$ with finite residue field in which the image of $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$ for $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$) to $\mathbb{C}$ carrying each such $T_\ell$ to $a_\ell(g)$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from its range to $O'$. Let $\rho$ be a two-dimensional $\lambda$-adic Galois representation over $O'$ (a free $O'$-module of rank $2$ with an adically continuous action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, realised as automorphisms of the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$) such that for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$ (lying in the decomposition subgroup and acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field), the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X + \ell$. Assume furthermore that every two-dimensional representation over any characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring $O''$ with finite residue field that is a module-finite local $O'$-algebra with injective structure map, and whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at all primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \neq \lambda$ are $X^2 - \iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X + \ell$ over $O''$, has residual representation absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to the algebraic closure of the residue field) and odd (every element of order two has determinant $-1$). Then: first, for every prime $q \neq \lambda$ whose exponent in $M$ is exactly $2$, $\rho$ is not unipotent on inertia at $q$, i.e. there are a valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $P$ and an element $\sigma$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with $\mathrm{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma)) \neq (X-1)^2$; and second, for every prime $q \neq \lambda$ with $q \mid M$ and $q^2 \nmid M$, every valuation subring $A$ over $q$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $q$ for $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - (q+1)X + q$ or $X^2 + (q+1)X + q$.
--
--   This records the local behaviour at primes of bad reduction of the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two newform: Steinberg shape (Frobenius eigenvalues $\pm 1, \pm q$) at primes exactly dividing the level, and failure of unipotence on inertia at primes whose exponent in the level is two. It is used in the identification of the local types of the representation attached to an elliptic curve with those of a newform of the expected level, feeding [`WeierstrassCurve.isModularModelOfLevel_conductorLevel_of_not_cube_dvd_of_modRepIsIrreducible_of_factorization_eq`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.isModularModelOfLevel_conductorLevel_of_not_cube_dvd_of_modRepIsIrreducible_of_factorization_eq).
